["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0d3bf-067c-7068-af65-bd964ce78fcb","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"## Context\n\nThe 0.36.2 release gate failed after all product changes landed because parallel PostgreSQL tests each opened an ER store in `public` solely to drop their private schema. Those incidental migrations raced in PostgreSQL's type catalog even though every test's actual data schema was isolated.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nSchema cleanup remains test-only, serializes the shared public-schema connection, the complete gate passes with PostgreSQL enabled, and the corrected patch is published without moving the failed 0.36.2 tag.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe PostgreSQL backend test module now serializes only its shared cleanup helper. Each product test still runs in parallel against a private schema, while the incidental `public`-schema migration used to obtain a drop handle can no longer race another cleanup. The backend suite passed ten consecutive live runs and the complete gate passed with PostgreSQL enabled.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-8170552df80fd80901883291b6895eb0","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/postgres-test-schema-cleanup-race","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nThe 0.36.2 release gate failed after all product changes landed because parallel PostgreSQL tests each opened an ER store in `public` solely to drop their private schema. Those incidental migrations raced in PostgreSQL's type catalog even though every test's actual data schema was isolated.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nSchema cleanup remains test-only, serializes the shared public-schema connection, the complete gate passes with PostgreSQL enabled, and the corrected patch is published without moving the failed 0.36.2 tag.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe PostgreSQL backend test module now serializes only its shared cleanup helper. Each product test still runs in parallel against a private schema, while the incidental `public`-schema migration used to obtain a drop handle can no longer race another cleanup. The backend suite passed ten consecutive live runs and the complete gate passed with PostgreSQL enabled.\n","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Prevent parallel test cleanup from racing migrations in the shared public schema.","title":"PostgreSQL backend tests serialize shared cleanup"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"summary":"Prevent parallel test cleanup from racing migrations in the shared public schema.","title":"PostgreSQL backend tests serialize shared cleanup"},"id":"ent-8170552df80fd80901883291b6895eb0","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-8170552df80fd80901883291b6895eb0"]}]